From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ws2_32, server, ntdll: setsockopt(SO_ERROR) and TransmitPackets

- setsockopt(SO_ERROR) was a stub that dropped the value; it is kept with
  the socket now (a new IOCTL_AFD_WINE_SET_SO_ERROR) and getsockopt(SO_ERROR)
  gives it back, as on Windows, until it is set to 0 (then the socket's own
  pending error is reported again). A value shorter than an int:
  WSAEFAULT. Wine's sock test's todo passes.
- TransmitPackets is given by SIO_GET_EXTENSION_FUNCTION_POINTER
  (WSAID_TRANSMITPACKETS was commented out, so callers got WSAEINVAL): it
  sends its elements in order, memory buffers and file ranges (from an
  offset, -1 for the file's own position, a length of 0 for the rest of
  the file), in pieces of nSendSize, waits on a non-blocking socket, and
  with TF_DISCONNECT or TF_REUSE_SOCKET disconnects after them. An
  overlapped call completes with the bytes sent: IOCTL_AFD_WINE_COMPLETE_ASYNC
  takes the transfer count beside the status now.
- An unknown extension GUID is a warning, not a FIXME.

Gate: test/sockmisc-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/sockmisc-probe.c). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_SO_ERROR_IGNORED (server/sock.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_TRANSMIT
(ws2_32/socket.c).
